# Change Scope Discipline

- Do not change behavior that is already working unless the user explicitly asks to modify that part.
- Keep edits tightly scoped to the request; avoid replacing adjacent components, flows, or patterns just because another implementation also works.
- Before touching a working area that may be affected by the requested change, call out the risk and explain why that area needs to be touched.
- When fixing one issue, preserve the current behavior of nearby features unless the user asks for a broader cleanup or refactor.
